 and ${x}_{l}=a+lΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}2{x}^{-4}\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=2{x}^{-4},$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=4.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-(1)}{n}=\\frac{3}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}2{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{l})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[f(1+l\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[f(1+\\frac{3l}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[2{(1+\\frac{3l}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73159/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdc82e49-5df6-5096-a8fd-e00017fb1e3a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73159"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346179/field-1/b2847075d2c5b715e7419c5ab724da65ed0d37b2aac450c565bb0c2452dbf80e" :answer/id #uuid "30f82af4-a1b4-5824-8336-f716548cdc63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2i}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346179/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "56401737-9f0d-5ff7-af83-3bf5e5047657" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346179/field-1/b2847075d2c5b715e7419c5ab724da65ed0d37b2aac450c565bb0c2452dbf80e" :answer-field/choices ["q-346179/field-1/b2847075d2c5b715e7419c5ab724da65ed0d37b2aac450c565bb0c2452dbf80e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346179/field-2/b2847075d2c5b715e7419c5ab724da65ed0d37b2aac450c565bb0c2452dbf80e" :answer/id #uuid "958d273c-e6ff-5856-a66e-fef248a41117" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2i}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346179/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "29474782-597b-53f8-90e6-756891c36b52" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346179/field-2/b2847075d2c5b715e7419c5ab724da65ed0d37b2aac450c565bb0c2452dbf80e" :answer-field/choices ["q-346179/field-2/b2847075d2c5b715e7419c5ab724da65ed0d37b2aac450c565bb0c2452dbf80e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346179" :question/id #uuid "48803847-d9e3-51f7-a9db-8dadbd254933" :question/math-academy-id "q-346179" :question/problem "Express ${\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{3}+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x$ as the limit of a left Riemann sum.\n\n*Hint: Write down the missing expression in terms of $i$ and $n.$*\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{3}+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[(($\n{{field-1}}\n$)^{3}+2($\n{{field-2}}\n$)+1)\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]$" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{3}+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)={x}^{3}+2x+1,$ the lower bound is $a=0,$ and the upper bound is $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-0}{n}=\\frac{2}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{3}+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(0+i\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(\\frac{2i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[({(\\,\\frac{2i}{n}\\,)}^{3}+2(\\,\\frac{2i}{n}\\,)+1)\\,\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-346179/field-1" "q-346179/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdc82e49-5df6-5096-a8fd-e00017fb1e3a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346179"] 